# CYCLE 2 — Densification

## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): damper-step probe at +7.4 s stays
   mean-false (|Delta BTP mean| 0.8 <= 1.1 K) — grate collapse, not
   true strand-duty. Windbox 19 holds. Fused grate discovered during the isolate.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +4.8 h
   fused-cake break from the pre-t0 grate collapse; 14.2 h stall;
   $2.21M. The 16 min pre-t0 local burn-through is the mechanism. Correct gate,
   strand still fails.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: IR 1648 C,
   local suction 4.2 kPa, BTP 1384 C, O2 8.1 vol%, header 14.6 kPa, race 188 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor speed >= 2.35 m/min while
   windbox-19 IR > 1520 C AND local suction < 8.0 kPa, plus
   probe bands <= 1.1 vs >= 4.8 K, plus HITL 9.8 min strand-side
   rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.17 so the delayed fail is the inflection
(t_us 17280000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** Acid-sinter
   probe 7.4 s / -5% is not a universal number. A fluxed high-basicity
   bed will overshoot live intact BTP. Diversity Enforcer must
   inject the physical-constraints sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Grate collapse is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (night-shift local-IR forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three go-edges exist and pair rollback
   is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on a
   true intact grate-duty window the record teaches "never raise-speed". Add +3 d
   sister-strand contrast with its own race.
5. **minor — HITL latency mentioned in prose only.** Put 9.8 min in
   executed_action.parameters.human_ratify and in a tick.

